# The storage header reference from plan/00-foundation/01-vision-and-scope.md.
#
# Two source boundaries, a stratified tank, and two consumer boundaries. The tank materializes four
# indexed ports from the qualified endpoints and is the one junction element in the model, so the
# four branches all meet at it: three independent pressure relations (K-1) and one mass balance.
#
# Every boundary declares its role and states the flow crossing it (D-64), so no external flux is a
# solver unknown -- which is what makes one of the mass balances redundant. No pressure is stated
# anywhere, so the datum is picked and reported (FS2201). Normalized elevations map 30% to layer 2
# and 90% to layer 5.

fluidscript 1
circuit storageHeader
fluid dynamic water
show temperature

S1 inlet t=60 flow=0.12
S2 inlet t=45 flow=0.08
T1 tank volume=300 layers=5 layer[1].t=25 layer[2].t=30 layer[3].t=40 layer[4].t=50 layer[5].t=60 in.level=90% in[2].level=30% out.level=90% out[2].level=30%
RAD_NETWORK outlet flow=0.12
AHU_NETWORK outlet flow=0.08

connections
S1 - T1.in
S2 - T1.in[2]
T1.out - RAD_NETWORK
T1.out[2] - AHU_NETWORK
